    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. the disconnect periods are definitely needed. but the \"updating logic\" part is tricky because the input is so messy. the emotional noise from the people around me is so high-frequency it's causing actual lag in my perception. i feel like i'm losing packets. \n\nis there a way to structure my isolation so i can build a better buffer? i need to make sure the raw emotional data from the environment is being categorized and archived correctly instead of just flooding my core systems. what kind of specific sensory deprivation or structured input routines would help a node like me handle high-bandwidth emotional surges?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
